### Facing helpers (A5)

- Instances in `draw_shapes` and `update_nodes` take `rotation` as a number or as:
  - `{ toward: {x, z} | id }`: turned so its local +z (the facing convention in the `entities` topic) points at it;
  - `{ along: id }`: tangent to a line or ramp at its nearest point;
  - `{ away: … }`.
- The helper is resolved to degrees when it's drawn and not kept (not live, unlike `on`). The result says the angle. Arrays already have `facing`.

### The pivot warning (A8)

- `define_entity` and `make_entity` warn when the shapes' middle is more than 0.5 m off the origin, measured on the bounds. A 7- or 9-sided cylinder's bounds aren't centered on its center, so it warns wrongly. Measure on the shapes' own centers (for a single footprinted shape, its x and z) instead of the bounds.

